<script lang="ts">
    import TypedCounter from './TypedCounter.svelte'
    const { data }: { data: { greeting: string, start: number } } = $props()
    let changes = $state(0)
</script>

# Build-time markdown, runtime renderers

{#snippet greeting(text)}
    <p data-testid="load-greeting">{text}</p>
{/snippet}

This **bold text**, [reference link][shared], and table use our existing renderer.

| Stage | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| Parsing | Build |
| Rendering | SvelteMarkdown |

<section data-testid="compiled-island">
    <h2>Compiled Svelte</h2>
    {@render greeting(data.greeting)}
    <TypedCounter start={data.start} details={{ label: 'typed object' }} onchange={() => changes++} />
    <p data-testid="parent-changes">Parent updates: {changes}</p>
    {#if changes > 0}<p data-testid="conditional">Compiled control flow works</p>{/if}
</section>

Inline page data: **{`${data.greeting}`}**.

## Markdown after the compiled island

This second [reference link][shared] shares definitions with the first.

```svelte
<Counter start={6} />
```

